Here circles are

$$

\begin{array}{l}

x^{2}+y^{2}-2 x-2 y=0...(1) \\

x^{2}+y^{2}=4...(2) \\

\text { Now, } \mathrm{C}_{1}(1,1), r_{1}=\sqrt{1^{2}+1^{2}}=\sqrt{2} \\

C_{2}(0,0), r_{2}=2

\end{array}

$$

If $\theta$ is the angle of intersection then

$$

\begin{array}{l}

\cos \theta=\frac{r_{1}^{2}+r_{2}^{2}-\left(c_{1} c_{2}\right)^{2}}{2 r_{1} r_{2}} \\

=\frac{2+4-(\sqrt{2})^{2}}{2 \cdot \sqrt{2.2}}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} \Rightarrow \theta=45^{\circ}

\end{array}

$$
